    description: "WHAT. Left open in haskell.py after PR #2329 (instances record their class; symbols carry <Module>.<name>):\n- instance Yesod (App a) / instance Yesod [Foo] keep the class-only name \"Yesod\", and a second such instance of one class in a file is dropped (seen_names); fixing the names moves stable ids.\n- newtype emits no symbol; a standalone deriving instance emits none; deriving clauses are not recorded.\n- Methods inside an instance body are not symbols, so a hosted_application entry on an instance has an empty forward slice.\n- On the yesod framework repository 18 hosted_application entries (many of them test-fixture apps) displace 9 main_function entries under the 50-entry cap.\n- Not measured on a mixed repository: a reference with no host language can now be answered at the qualified tier by a Haskell <Module>.<name>; framework_patterns._get_parent_class_name returns the module for a Haskell function (read only by JAX-RS / prefix_from_parent rows).\n\nFound during PR #2329 (2026-11-22). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/three_pr_plan_11222026/pr2/RESULTS.md and RESIDUALS_TO_FILE.md."  # 4c15
